{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nGerrit change 1869 patch set 1 (revision dcb219a7408e2ebeb68d3a17c97df4907b28ba2d) failed its sole macOS/Python 3.13 job in GitHub Actions run 32187810048. The failed test was tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py::test_session_finish_fails_explicitly_when_porcelain_times_out: its nested pytest subprocess exceeded the test harness's 12-second outer deadline even though captured stderr showed the intended internal git status --porcelain watchdog raising subprocess.TimeoutExpired after 5 seconds. The rest of the run passed (13,880 passed, 65 skipped); Ubuntu 3.11/3.12/3.13 all passed.\n\nThis ticket is intentionally separate from change 1869. The observed 5-second internal watchdog plus 12-second outer deadline is only a lead: investigate dynamically whether macOS teardown/scheduling overhead, product liveness, or unrelated infrastructure explains the failure.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce the real nested-pytest harness under controlled scheduling/teardown delays and capture the runtime path from the five-second Git watchdog through pytest session-finish cleanup.\n- Generate and run falsifiable experiments that distinguish harness-budget exhaustion from a product watchdog failure and from unrelated runner infrastructure.\n- After a proven RCA, encode the final observable timeout contract with a held-out RED oracle, repair via an independent fixer, then prove GREEN, exact-defect mutation RED, and original-report replication.\n- Sweep sibling nested-process deadline tests for the same budget-coupling pattern.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Runtime evidence proves a specific, changeable root cause and rules out product-watchdog and unrelated-infrastructure alternatives.\n- [ ] A final-form held-out regression test is observed RED before repair and GREEN afterward.\n- [ ] Reintroducing the exact defect returns the oracle to RED, then restoring the repair returns it to GREEN.\n- [ ] The original nested-pytest blocking-Git scenario completes reliably with the intended explicit watchdog failure under controlled macOS-equivalent teardown overhead.\n- [ ] Relevant focused tests plus lint and typecheck pass.\n- [ ] Sibling timing-contract occurrences are swept and every confirmed sibling is fixed or ticketed.\n\n## Expected file impact\n- tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787090747142011001,"uuid":"67ad0550-72e2-4cab-826b-a9142d0a4271"}